// SECI-FDRE-X: assured peak supply of 4800 MWh (1200 MW x 4 h) from ISTS-connected RE projects with
// storage, sold to SECI under a 25-year Power Purchase Agreement. Every term below is taken from the
// tender documents: the RfS, the standard PPA, the standard PSA (SECI with the Buying Entity) and
// Amendment-01, which deletes clauses of the PPA and the PSA. Each cites its document, clause and
// page and quotes it word for word (tests/engine/test_fdrex_terms.py checks every quote against its
// page; all four PDFs are in web/public/tenders/seci-fdre-x/ and are served from there).
// Pages are the page numbers printed on the document. The RfS prints "Page 16 of 138" and its PDF has
// a cover first, so its PDF page is the printed page + 1 (pdfOffset; `pages` is the printed count, the
// PDF has 139). The PPA ("Page 28 of 84"), the PSA ("Page 20 of 33") and Amendment-01 ("Page 2 of 7")
// print the PDF page itself, so they carry no offset.
// Where Amendment-01 deleted a clause, the original is kept, marked "replaced" (with `by`: the
// document that replaced it), next to a term that quotes the amendment. Where the documents differ,
// the term is marked "conflict" and its `flag` says what differs; the PPA read with the PSA prevails
// over the RfS (PPA 1.2.18, the term "precedence"). A "conflict" of another kind (a reference that
// leads nowhere, or two clauses of one document that pull apart) says so in its `flag`, and may carry
// its own `badge`.

